# Large, regenerable data/embedding artifacts -- not source, don't commit.
# Not all of it is disposable scratch, though: load.py's rna_X.npy/prot_X.npy
# are cheap to regenerate, but scanvi_run.py and scanvi_run_pbmc240.py's own
# outputs (rna_scanvi_seed{N}.npy, prot_scanvi_seed{N}.npy,
# pbmc_scanvi_seed{N}.npy, the pred_*_seed{N}.npy prediction arrays, and
# result_scanvi*_seed{N}.json) are the product of real scVI/scANVI training
# runs (each on the order of an hour) -- don't delete those without
# regenerating first if you need them again; nothing else in this repo
# reproduces them, only the two scripts that wrote them.
results/
*.log
__pycache__/
